---
import CodeBlock from '@/components/code-block.astro'
import Docs from '@/layouts/Docs.astro'

import { Callout, Link, Table } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'
---

<Docs
  title="Agent Skills"
  description="Install Astro Doctor's portable skill and optional Claude Code and Cursor hooks so coding agents have the project rules at hand."
  editPath="apps/docs/src/pages/docs/agent-skills.astro"
>
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <h1>Agent skills</h1>
    <p class="docs-page-lead">
      Give your coding agent the same Astro patterns your checks enforce. The installer copies
      one portable skill into your project, with optional hooks for Claude Code and Cursor.
    </p>
  </header>

  <h2>Install the skill</h2>

  <CodeBlock code="pnpm dlx @santi020k/astro-doctor@latest install" language="bash" />

  <p>
    Run the command from your project root. It writes <code>skills/astro-doctor.md</code>,
    offers to create a GitHub Actions workflow, and can install native agent hooks.
    Use <code>--dry-run</code> to preview the file changes first.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`pnpm dlx @santi020k/astro-doctor@latest install --dry-run
pnpm dlx @santi020k/astro-doctor@latest install --agent-hooks`}
    label="Preview and agent hooks"
    language="bash"
  />

  <Table aria-label="Installed agent skill files" role="region" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Destination</th><th>When it is installed</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>skills/astro-doctor.md</code></td>
          <td>Every install; reference it from your agent's project instructions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>.claude/skills/astro-doctor.md</code></td>
          <td>With <code>--agent-hooks</code> or after accepting the native hooks prompt.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>.cursor/rules/astro-doctor.mdc</code></td>
          <td>With <code>--agent-hooks</code> or after accepting the native hooks prompt.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Table>

  <Callout>
    <strong>Keep your context current:</strong> Commit the installed skill with your project.
    Re-running the installer replaces its skill files with the current bundled version, so review
    any local edits before updating.
  </Callout>

  <h2>What the skill covers</h2>
  <p>
    The portable skill explains Astro Doctor checks with code examples: island hydration,
    image optimization, accessible markup, safe HTML and environment variables, content
    collections, and project configuration. It also documents scanning and CI workflows.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask your agent to explain a finding before changing a component.</li>
    <li>Use the examples to choose a fix that fits your page.</li>
    <li>Run Astro Doctor again to verify the result.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reference it from your agent</h2>
  <p>
    For agents that read a project instructions file, reference the installed Markdown file.
    The Claude Code and Cursor hooks contain the same skill when you enable them.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`Read skills/astro-doctor.md before editing Astro components.
After changing a component, run Astro Doctor and address relevant findings.`}
    label="Project instructions example"
    language="text"
  />

  <h2>Repository resources</h2>
  <p>
    Astro Doctor's repository also contains contributor skills for rule implementation and Astro
    performance. These files are separate from the portable skill installed by the CLI.
    Browse them directly or copy the resources you need:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/astro-doctor/tree/main/.agents/skills/astro-rules" newTab>
        Astro rules reference
      </Link> — rule patterns and examples.
    </li>
    <li>
      <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/astro-doctor/tree/main/.agents/skills/astro-performance" newTab>
        Astro performance guide
      </Link> — hydration, images, View Transitions, and server islands.
    </li>
    <li>
      <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/astro-doctor/tree/main/.agents/skills/add-rule" newTab>
        Add a rule
      </Link> — the repository's test-driven contribution workflow.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Callout>
    <strong>Project overview:</strong> The repository's
    <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/astro-doctor/blob/main/llms.txt" newTab><code>llms.txt</code></Link>
    provides additional context about Astro Doctor and its packages.
  </Callout>
</Docs>
